<title>BELGIUM: BBL 1996 group net profit up 15.1 pct.</title>
<headline>BBL 1996 group net profit up 15.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full-year 1996</p>
<p>(billions Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net (excludes minorities)	  10.29 vs	8.94</p>
<p>    Cons net					 10.40 vs	9.02</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)			 190  vs	 175</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name Banque Bruxelles Lambert SA (BBL).  </p>
<p>    Cons net interest income		   54.35 vs     49.24</p>
<p>    Cons sundry income			   32.77 vs     25.75</p>
<p>    Total operating revenue		    87.13 vs     74.99</p>
<p>    General administrative expenses	  53.09 vs     47.19</p>
<p>	Salaries, social security costs	36.37 vs     32.52</p>
<p>	Other administrative expenses	  16.72 vs     14.67</p>
<p>    Gross operating income		     34.03 vs     27.80</p>
<p>    Depreciation, write-downs, provisions  13.82 vs     13.10</p>
<p>	Of which on loans			   4.62 vs	6.35</p>
<p>	Transfer to general banking risk fund 2.32 vs     nil</p>
<p>    Pretax profit				  17.90 vs     14.71</p>
<p>    Balance sheet assets		    3,604    vs  3,225</p>
<p>    Customer deposits			 1,801    vs  1,610</p>
<p>    Private sector credits		  1,325    vs  1,162</p>
<p>    Public sector credits		     936    vs    852</p>
<p>    Shareholder funds			    89.4  vs     79.7</p>
<p>    Tier one capital ratio		  6.59 pct vs  6.69 pct</p>
<p>    Total capital ratio		    11.09 pct vs 11.00 pct</p>
<p>    Return on equity			 12.17 pct vs 11.81 pct</p>
<p>    Cost/income ratio			60.94 pct vs 62.03 pct</p>
<p>Note - BBL said that among the most significant modifications within the consolidation scope is the full integration of French stock brokerage Ferri, in which BBL has a majority stake since June 1996.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
